      "body": "## Motivation\n\nLarge local diffusion replies are spilled to a private `.npy` file in the request's shared-memory directory. When the client materializes the reply, `NumpyArrayFileRef.materialize` calls `np.load`, which reads the whole payload into a second host allocation before the file is unlinked. A 124-frame 1344x768 video reply carries about 1.54 GB of FP32 data through this path.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `NumpyArrayFileRef.materialize` loads the spill with `mmap_mode=\"c\"` and returns a plain `np.ndarray` view over the mapping. Pages are read when the consumer touches them instead of up front.\n- The mapping outlives the unlink that follows and the request-directory cleanup. Copy-on-write keeps the returned array writable without modifying the file.\n- Trade-off: a retained reply keeps its spill storage and one mapping alive until the last view is released, instead of owning an independent allocation.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo numerical change: the returned array holds the same bytes as before. `test_materialized_spill_is_a_writable_mapping` checks that the result is backed by a mapping, that the spill file is removed, and that writes to the result work without changing the other values.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThe end-to-end effect is small. The one-line form has not been benchmarked on a model. An earlier, larger variant of the same idea (a writable mapping with free-space and descriptor guards) was measured on H200 with a 124-frame video model (one warmup, then three 50-step requests per variant, at `49933325`):\n\n| Stage | Before | After |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Client reply materialization | ~0.59 s | ~0.0005 s |\n| Client uint8 conversion (full pass over the data) | 0.34 s | 0.34 s |\n| Whole request, generate call to host media | 304.746 s | 303.973 s |\n\nThe producer side (writing the spill) is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). `test_ipc_array.py`: 20 passed on this branch.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not applicable.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40206012613](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40206012613)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40206012606](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40206012606)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40206012646](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40206012646)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
