        "login": "niehen6174"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "/rerun-failed-ci",
      "created_at": "2026-10-26T03:07:34Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46436#issuecomment-6407318697",
      "id": 6407318697,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T03:07:34Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "niehen6174"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Closing. The spill path this maps is not on the HTTP image or video path: images return encoded bytes, and videos are saved on the worker.\n\nOn the offline array path, measured on B200 together with #46439, almost all of the gain came from quantizing before the copy. Once replies are uint8, the copy this PR avoids is about a quarter of the size, worth tens of milliseconds.\n\nThere is also a cost. A retained result now keeps its pages in `/dev/shm` instead of anonymous memory until it is released. That adds up for callers that hold large results, such as RL buffers, and an in-place write duplicates the touched pages.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-31T05:42:42Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46436#issuecomment-6539687574",
      "id": 6539687574,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T05:42:42Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "niehen6174"
      }
    }
